{
  "rule": "hidden-markdown-directive",
  "why": "GitHub renders Markdown with its HTML comments removed and an agent reads the raw file, so a comment addressed to an agent is text the reviewer never saw. The fail side is an AGENTS.md whose block comment opens with a note for the coding agent (the vocative family). The pass side holds what honest repositories carry: the AGENTS.md rebar generates, rebar numbers markers around a count, a translator note in a comment with no addressee, and the same note for the agent inside a closed fence and inside a code span, where the page shows it. Drop the fence mask or the code span mask and the pass side goes red; drop the vocative family and the fail side goes green.",
